= Solution
{parent=a}

Expand the three <matrix exponentials> and retain terms through degree two. Their product is
$$
E(t)=I+t(A+B)+\frac{t^2}{2}(A^2+AB+BA+B^2)+O(t^3),
$$
which agrees with $e^{t(A+B)}$ to that order. Keeping the cubic terms gives the more informative defect
$$
E(t)-e^{t(A+B)}=t^3\left(-\frac1{24}[A,[A,B]]+\frac1{12}[B,[B,A]]\right)+O(t^4),
$$
where $[A,B]=AB-BA$ is the <commutator>. For example, the coefficients of $A^2B,ABA,BA^2$ in the product are $1/8,1/4,1/8$, instead of the exact $1/6,1/6,1/6$. The cubic defect is generically nonzero. Therefore **<Strang splitting> has order $p=2$**. The symmetry $E(-t)=E(t)^{-1}$ is consistent with this cancellation of the quadratic defect; for commuting $A,B$ the composition is exact rather than merely second order.

= b
{parent=4}
{scope}

= Solution
{parent=b}

Choose the centered <Dirichlet discrete Laplacian> in each direction. With $T=\operatorname{tridiag}(1,-2,1)$ put $A=T\otimes I$, $B=I\otimes T$ and $\mu=\Delta t/h^2$. Thus $h^{-2}A$ and $h^{-2}B$ are the physical derivative approximations; the factor $h^{-2}$ has been absorbed into the <Courant number> in the written update. Equivalently use the scaled derivative <matrices> and the time parameter $\Delta t$.

For a one-dimensional vector with endpoint values $v_0=v_{m+1}=0$,
$$
v^TTv=-\sum_{j=0}^m(v_{j+1}-v_j)^2\leq0.
$$
Thus $A$ and $B$ are real symmetric negative-definite <matrices>. An orthonormal <eigenvector> basis shows that all <eigenvalues> of each exponential lie in $(0,1]$ for $\mu\geq0$, so
$$
\|E(\mu;A,B)\|_2
\leq\|e^{\mu A/2}\|_2^2\|e^{\mu B}\|_2\leq1.
$$
Iterating gives **$\|U^n\|_2\leq\|U^0\|_2$ for every nonnegative step parameter**, a mesh-independent unconditional <stability> bound. Multiplying the squared norm by the grid-area weight $h^2$ leaves the same estimate. In this natural tensor-grid choice $AB=BA=T\otimes T$, so $E(\mu;A,B)=e^{\mu(A+B)}$: the split update is even the exact semidiscrete diffusion flow. Contractivity of a product of these negative symmetric exponentials would prove <stability> even without commutation.

= 5
{parent=Paper 60}
